# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12: Counter's body catches mk's Oops as a method's body does -- v is 5 + 2
# = 7 after an execution from the root and again from a method.  A procedure lists no throws, so what
# its body does not catch is refused at the call (unit_named_struct_throw_refused).  Entry 7.
fn: mk () int
    throws: Oops
    if: 1 = 1
        throw: Oops(5)
    return: 1
end: mk
Counter:
    int: v 0
    ---
        v: mk()
        catch: Oops (int: w)
            v: w + 2
    ---
return
fn: run () int
    Counter
    int: r 0
    r: Counter\v
return: r
Counter
int: a 0
a: Counter\v
int: ok 0
if: a = 7 && run() = 7
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
